From 0bafb2d90972985c0c31c00e528cbb7dd2757b87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chandan <chandan@medpath.dev>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 10:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Test Order: follow-up fixes (progress trail, age display,
 collapsible sections, CTA spacing)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Order progress now matches the Registration page's compact dot +
  connector workflow-trail (in the page header) instead of the
  standalone timeline card, for visual consistency across screens.
- Patient age now shows a full breakdown — '19 Years - 11 Months -
  16 Days' — instead of a single year count, via a new
  PatientFlowService.calcAgeParts() helper. Gender is now prefixed
  with a gender icon (male/female/other) instead of plain text.
- Popular Tests and Frequently Ordered Packages are now collapsed by
  default with a Show/Hide toggle in each card header, instead of
  always rendering open.
- Fixed 'Save & Continue to Billing' spacing: the Ctrl+Enter kbd
  hint was using margin-left:auto inside a centered flex button,
  which threw off the centering of the label itself. The label is
  now its own centered group and the kbd hint is positioned as a
  small corner badge, with proper left/right padding at the 52px
  button height.
